    }

    // Count fixed points and cycles in the mapping x -> x^k mod n
    // For each cycle of length d, the number of valid assignments is n^(gcd(k-1, d)) if certain conditions hold

    // Actually, the correct approach:
    // For each x, we have the constraint f(x^k) = f(x)^k
    // This creates constraints on the values of f

